# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPLATE -- to ADD a publication:
#
#  1. Find (or create) the "== YEAR" section. New years go at the TOP of the
#     page; inside a year, journal papers come before conference papers.
#  2. Copy the three blocks below, paste them at the END of the matching
#     "=== Journal papers" or "=== Conference papers" list, and edit.
#  3. Leave ONE BLANK LINE between the citation and the ~~~ lines, and one
#     blank line after the closing ~~~.
#  4. Run:  python build.py       (this also regenerates files/publications.bib)
#
# +J5+ *P. L. Vo*, N. X. Author, "Title of the paper," /Journal Name/,
# vol. 1, no. 2, pp. 3--14, 2027.
#
# ~~~
# {BibTeX}{bibtex}
# @article{vo2027shortkey,
#   author  = {Vo, P. L. and Author, N. X.},
#   title   = {Title of the paper},
#   journal = {Journal Name},
#   volume  = {1},
#   number  = {2},
#   pages   = {3--14},
#   year    = {2027}
# }
# ~~~
#
# NOTE ABOUT SORTING: jemdoc does not sort anything. The order you see is the
# order in this file, so simply put new entries where you want them to appear.
# Keep the years in descending order (2027, 2026, 2025, ...).
#
